# Line endings are part of the contract.
#
# A statement's identity is sha256 over its canonical bytes, and a corpus is pinned
# by sha256 of the file. If a Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF in a corpus file,
# every anchor in the repository fails with S2_HASH_MISMATCH — the tool is right and
# the clone is wrong. These rules make a fresh clone byte-identical to the pinned
# content, so the first experience is a pass rather than a mystery.
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pinned corpora are bytes, not text: no conversion on checkout or commit.
corpus/** -text

*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
